Interview Preparation – 1 to 2 Years Experience (DevOps / Cloud)

If you have 1–2 years of experience, interviewers mostly test fundamentals + real understanding, not fancy tools.

Here are must-prepare interview questions 👇

• What is DevOps and why do companies use it?
• Difference between CI and CD?
• What happens in a typical CI/CD pipeline?
• Git vs GitHub – what’s the difference?
• How do you resolve a Git merge conflict?
• What is a Git branch and why do we use it?
• What is Docker and why is it used?
Difference between Docker image and container?
• What is a Dockerfile?
• What is Docker Compose?
• Why do we use Kubernetes?
• What is a Pod in Kubernetes?
• Difference between Deployment and Service?
• What is a Namespace in Kubernetes?
• What is AWS EC2 and why do we use it?
• Difference between EC2 and Lambda?
• What is Auto Scaling in AWS?
• What is IAM and why is it important?
• Difference between IAM Role and IAM User?
• What is S3 and common use cases?
• Difference between public and private S3 buckets?
. What is monitoring and why is it important?
• Difference between logs and metrics?
• What is Linux? Name some basic Linux commands
• How do you check disk usage in Linux?
• What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC)?
• What is Terraform and why is it used?
• Difference between Terraform plan and apply?
• What is state file in Terraform?
• What is Jenkins and why is it used?
• What is a Jenkins pipeline?
• Difference between freestyle job and pipeline?
• What is a build artifact?
• What is Blue-Green deployment?
What is Rolling deployment?
• What is Load Balancer?
• Difference between ALB and NLB?
• What is VPC in AWS?
• Difference between public and private subnet?
• What is Security Group?
• Difference between Security Group and NACL?
• What is DNS and why do we use it?
• What is Route 53?
• What is CloudWatch?
• What is an AMI?
• What is a cron job?
• What is bash scripting?
• What is a package manager in Linux?
• What is systemd?
What challenges have you faced in your current project?

💡 Tip for 1–2 years experience candidates:
Clear explanation of your project + tools + problems you solved matters more than buzzwords.

